---
title: Spicy cumin potatoes
servings: 2
tags: [vegan, quick]
source: Spicy cumin potatoes by Woon Heng, https://woonheng.com/spicy-cumin-potatoes
---

Rinse the @potatoes{1%lb}(small baby, skin on) well.

Steam ~{15-20%minutes} until a toothpick slides through. Let cool ~{5%minutes}, until you can handle them.

Press each potato flat with the bottom of a glass or the side of a wide knife. Halve any big ones first so they are all about the same thickness.

Heat the @cooking oil{2%tbsp} in a #wok{} over medium heat. Fry the potatoes ~{3-4%minutes} a side, letting a crust form before turning. Lift out.

Add a little more @cooking oil{} if needed. Fry the @dried chiles{2}(cut into pieces) and @cumin seeds{1/2%tsp} ~{20-30%seconds} until they sizzle and smell good; do not let them burn.

Put the potatoes back. Sprinkle over the @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @chili powder{1/2%tsp} and a pinch of @salt{}, and toss gently to coat.

Add the @light soy sauce{1%tbsp} and toss ~{1-2%minutes} more. Taste and add soy or salt if needed.

Turn off the heat. Toss in the @cilantro{1%tbsp}(stalks, chopped) and @?sesame seeds{1%tbsp}, and serve hot.
